      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/24/history-of-kawkawlin-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Jackson, Lansing & Saginaw Railroad reached Kawkawlin in 1871, shifting the town’s economy from river to rail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2026/04/24/history-of-kawkawlin-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kawkawlin began in 1844 when a sawmill sprang up on the riverbank, setting the course for the township’s growth.",
